WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:03.058
(electronic music)

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.173
- All right, this is the pilot of Lucifer.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.103
Act one.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.500
Exterior, City of Angels,
Sunset Boulevard, night.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.291
A jet black vintage sports
car sales down Sunset

00:00:18.291 --> 00:00:20.330
cruising through the adult Disneyland

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.670
that is nighttime Los Angeles.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.480
Neon and billboards
reflected on the windshield,

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.247
the Stones' "Gimme Shelter"
blasting from the radio, or-

00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:30.054
- Cause we couldn't afford it.

00:00:30.054 --> 00:00:32.547
(everyone laughing)

00:00:32.547 --> 00:00:35.133
- Or "No Rest For The
Wicked" by Cage the Elephant.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.620
Interior, Lucifer's car,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.360
behind the wheel the devil himself.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.250
Say hello to Lucifer Morningstar.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.830
He's good-looking, a
man of wealth and taste,

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.210
but that's not what makes
him jump off the screen.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.860
It's his vibe.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:54.860
Pure lusty mischief, sardonic
smile, timeless style.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.090
And yes, he's that
Lucifer, the son of God.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.530
The one who rebelled,
plotted against his father

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.290
and plummeted from grace.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.000
The one who was banished from paradise

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.070
and forced to serve as the
Lord of hell for all eternity.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.520
Right now Lucifer's was getting
pulled over for speeding.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.930
Motorcycle cop.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.240
Lucifer adjust his mirror
to see Officer Diggs

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.190
approaching the car.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:16.633
He yells over the music.

00:01:18.172 --> 00:01:19.922
- Can you turn down the music, sir?

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.053
- Ah, you know what they say, officer,

00:01:23.053 --> 00:01:25.503
if it's getting too loud,
you're getting too old.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.700
- Do you know why I pulled you over?

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.310
- Obviously you felt the need to exercise

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.730
your limited power and punish me

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:33.770
for ignoring the speed limit.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.430
It's okay, I understand.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.410
I like to punish people too.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.957
Or at least I used to.

00:01:39.957 --> 00:01:42.490
- Do you have any idea
how fast you were going?

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.670
- Haven't a clue.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:45.680
I blame it on the Stones,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.220
they just make a man want to drive.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.203
You know what I mean?

00:01:50.014 --> 00:01:51.430
- Well, you know, sometimes

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:56.590
I put my siren on and
drive really, really fast,

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.030
but for no reason, you
know, just cause I can.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.300
- Right?

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.829
And why wouldn't you?

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:03.010
It's fun!

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.891
It feels good to get away
with something, doesn't it?

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:06.727
- [Diggs] Hmm.

00:02:06.727 --> 00:02:09.190
- (chuckling) It's okay, officer.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.440
People like to tell me things,

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.730
those deep, dark, naughty little desires

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.290
that are really on their minds.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.620
It's a gift.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.320
Must be something about this face.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.503
- License and registration.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.760
- [Lucifer] Coming right up.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.280
- Are you trying to bribe me, sir?

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:26.590
- Yes, of course.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.423
Why is that not enough?

00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:30.030
Here, just take more, it's only money.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.070
- It's against the law.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.770
- Oh you people are funny about your laws.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.670
You break the law sometimes don't you?

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.273
Yeah, do tell.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.913
- Well, sometimes,

00:02:42.789 --> 00:02:45.749
I'll pull a woman over
for a minor infraction

00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:49.334
and get it to flash me a
little something something.

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.334
- Oh you dirty dog, you.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.140
- Sometimes I let her off
with, you know, with a warning.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.070
Sometimes I don't.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.350
Sometimes other stuff happens.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.163
- Oh, LA's finest.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.423
You're tempted to keep that, aren't you?

00:03:06.423 --> 00:03:08.570
Yeah, so what are you
waiting for, permission?

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.850
Keep it!

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.317
Buy yourself something
pretty, you deserve it.

00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:14.817
But if you don't mind, I
really must be on my way.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.233
- Okay sir.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.200
Have a good evening.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.583
- You too, officer.

00:03:21.643 --> 00:03:23.320
- Officer Diggs walked away,

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.900
Lucifer readjusts his mirror

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.630
but this time we see a
flash of something strange,

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.540
a glimpse of Lucifer's true reflection,

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.730
almost too fast to even comprehend,

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.370
but enough to unsettle us

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.531
or not, because we decide to
not do that later in post.

00:03:36.531 --> 00:03:38.820
(everyone laughing)

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.360
Lucifer skims the radio and roars off

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.770
leaving one very dazed cop in his wake.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.250
As he goes, we see the
caddies rear vanity plate

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.717
which reads "FALL1N1".

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.440
Title card.
(actors humming)

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.060
Exterior, Lux, street night.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.530
Lucifer pulls up in front of his bar, Lux.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.120
Doesn't look like much from the outside

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.990
but there's a long line
of Hollywood hipsters

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.380
dying to get in.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.790
Inside Lux now a little
bit of hell on earth,

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.570
a living breathing tribute
to Lucifer's favorite things,

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.550
wine, women, and song.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.690
Lucifer glides through
soaking up the sights

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.410
and sounds of elegant debauchery

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.790
like a proud modern day Gatsby.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.230
His eyes land on the
exotic dark hair beauty

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.860
tending bar over yonder, Mazikeen.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.230
But she's always been
just Maze to Lucifer.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.820
She leans seductively with
her back against the bar,

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.600
doesn't turn around as
this for approaches,

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.023
speaks to him via a mirror.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.020
- Where have you been?

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.210
- Holed up at the Chateau

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.240
copulating with a woman named Faith.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.233
Ironic, isn't it?

00:04:43.848 --> 00:04:46.633
Oh, have I ever told you
how incredibly sexy you are

00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:49.229
when you can't control your emotions?

00:04:49.229 --> 00:04:51.820
- And what emotions might those be?

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.273
- Why jealousy, of course.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.390
- Try disappointment.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.420
- A young man suddenly rises
from where he's been kneeling

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:00.253
in front of Maze.

00:05:00.253 --> 00:05:01.240
Lucifer's eyebrows go up.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.390
Didn't see that coming.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.120
- Thank you, Patrick.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:05.953
You can go.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:08.853
What?

00:05:08.853 --> 00:05:09.980
I dropped something.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.915
Now, Lucifer I'm a big fan of sex.

00:05:11.915 --> 00:05:13.200
- Obviously.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.980
- But shouldn't you be
spending your valuable time

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.900
doing something more significant?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.783
You're the Lord of hell
for crying out loud.

00:05:20.783 --> 00:05:24.250
- I'm retired, Maze, I've
got nothing but time.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.480
- Maze stares at him for a beat

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.310
then senses something, as does Lucifer.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.400
A ripple in the drink she just poured.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.790
Time slows.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.700
Music and laughter
become warped and haunted

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.120
as everyone in the club slows

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.143
except Lucifer and Maze who share a look.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.667
- I think you have a visitor.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:39.850
(Lucifer sighing)

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.140
- And through the slow motion crowd,

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.870
Lucifer sees Amenadiel.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.220
The man has a steady and grim intensity.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.290
He's Lucifer's brother and an angel.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:49.160
Yep, majestic wings and everything.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.040
But Amenadiel is also a bad-ass.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.866
Last thing he radiates
is angelic goodness.

00:05:53.866 --> 00:05:57.130
- Amenadiel, how's it hanging big guy?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.210
Didn't you see the sign?

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.600
No angels allowed.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.943
No?

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:03.463
I'll make an exception
for you, on the house.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.730
- You've become quite ensconced

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.623
with this little hobby of yours.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.202
Your return to the underworld
has been requested.

00:06:14.202 --> 00:06:15.350
- Oh!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.690
Okay, let me check my calendar.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:18.523
Yeah, here it is.

00:06:18.523 --> 00:06:20.400
The 7th of never through to the 15th

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.350
of ain't going to happen.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.956
How does that work for you guys?

00:06:22.956 --> 00:06:24.460
(everyone chuckling)

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.190
See, I'm consistently
surprised by the whole

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.453
no sense of humor thing.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:30.850
Look, remind dad, I quit hell

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:34.460
because I was sick and tired
of playing a part in his play.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.480
I believe in free will

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:38.840
but not the tyranny of all
this predestination hoo hah.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.800
- I'll warn you against
disrespecting our father, Lucifer.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:42.633
- Yeah?

00:06:42.633 --> 00:06:44.670
Well, our father has been disrespecting me

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.640
since the beginning of time.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.040
So pot kettle, don't you think?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.040
- You are a mockery of everything divine.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.660
- Thank you.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.780
But lately I've been doing
a fair amount of thinking.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.940
Do you think I'm the devil
because I'm inherently evil

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.140
or simply because dear
old dad decided I was?

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.590
I mean isn't this a
classic case of labeling?

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.350
- What do you think happens
when the devil leaves hell?

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:10.030
All those demons, those tormented souls.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.500
Where do you think they go?

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.923
- Don't know, don't care, not my problem.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.733
Look, tell father I'm not going back.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:21.630
Consider the position oficially open.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.270
So you, my feathered
friend, are going to hell

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.470
- In a blink, Amenadiel's
wing is at Lucifer's throat.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.157
Ancient fuel fused in its tips.

00:07:30.157 --> 00:07:33.043
Lucifer's glass falls,
shatters, but he doesn't flinch.

00:07:33.909 --> 00:07:35.634
- Oh, go for it.

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:37.363
You think father's upset now?

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.173
- Father has been patient for five years.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.453
He will not be merciful much longer.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:51.350
- Threat planted, Amenadiel
withdraws and exits.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:54.040
And the club now slips
back into regular motion.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.620
Lucifer only now deflates.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.370
Amenadiel clearly rattles him.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.240
Exterior Lux, street night.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:03.240
Lucifer stands outside,
spinning a coin in his hand,

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.910
still thinking about his
conversation with Amenadiel,

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.340
when a taxi slows to a
stop in front of Lux.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.620
The rear window rolls down,
a beautiful hot mess appears.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.050
This is Delilah.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.440
Delilah is a fallen from grace pop star,

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.260
the crowd waiting in line
reacts like crowds do

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:22.020
when confronted with a super
famous person, tragic or not.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.590
Oohs and aahs and iPhones galore

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.833
but Delilah only has eyes for Lucifer.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.743
- Remember me?

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.810
- Yes, you're famous.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.423
Delilah, isn't it?

00:08:32.423 --> 00:08:34.720
Could I have your autograph?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.920
- If I can have a drink.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.760
- Back inside Lux, Lucifer
and Delilah sit at a booth.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:41.540
Maze hovers in the background.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.133
- So why'd you really come back?

00:08:44.133 --> 00:08:46.650
- I don't know, I guess I feel safe here.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:49.030
Reminds me of who I was

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:52.860
before everything got so big and messy.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.133
And for you.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.320
Sometimes I feel like

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:01.320
you were the only person who
was ever really honest with me.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.433
But I need to know something.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:07.603
- What's that?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.244
- Did I sell my soul to the devil?

00:09:11.244 --> 00:09:12.820
- Well, that would imply the devil

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.010
is actually interested in your soul.

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:16.730
That's the stuff of movies and TV.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:18.740
They always get it wrong.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.020
- Come on, you took me in
off the street, Lucifer.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.403
You let me sing up there anytime I wanted.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:26.820
It's so weird.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.970
I told you that I want it to be a star.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:33.310
And that's when things
started happening for me.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:36.733
And you do call yourself Lucifer.

00:09:36.733 --> 00:09:37.870
- Call me whatever you want

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.920
but I'm really just a patron of the arts.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.210
Look, honestly, I introduced
you to a few people

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.810
that owed me favors, that's all.

00:09:46.667 --> 00:09:48.000
- Do you think I'm talented?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.113
- Of course I do.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:52.370
You have one of the most beautiful voices

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:53.680
I've ever heard.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.410
It's sweet, dirty, sexy, soulful.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.483
I knew you were a star, I just
helped the world catch up.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.820
- Well, it certainly feels
very Faustian at times

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:07.660
because along with the good, ooh,

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.150
came a hell of a lot of bad.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.360
- Oh, so the devil made you do it?

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.280
The alcohol, the drugs,
the topless selfies?

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.943
Your choices are on you, my dear.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.340
- You're right, you're right.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.920
You are absolutely right.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:24.430
But the toxic relationships
were my biggest screw ups.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:27.103
God, I really do have
the worst taste in men.

00:10:27.103 --> 00:10:28.740
- You really do, darling.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.020
Jimmy Barnes?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.580
I can't believe you almost
married that sweaty little imp.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.210
- He produced my album!

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:36.400
You introduced us.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.940
- I suggested you work with
him, not sleep with him.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.927
- I got confused.

00:10:40.927 --> 00:10:43.430
- And then you left him at the altar.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.950
- Yeah, that was pretty rude of me.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.480
- Actually, I rather liked
that bit. (chuckling)

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.080
- He trapped me in the bathroom
at the Grammy's a month ago,

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.250
cried, said he wanted
to get back together.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.660
Then I hear he's marrying
some supermodel this weekend

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:56.830
and I'm jealous!

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.732
Oh, god, I am such a mess!

00:10:58.732 --> 00:11:02.258
- God has nothing to do with
your mess any more than I do.

00:11:02.258 --> 00:11:04.243
You didn't sell your soul, Delilah,

00:11:04.243 --> 00:11:06.530
but you do owe me a favor.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.230
Looks like it's time to settle up.

00:11:09.473 --> 00:11:10.400
- I'm scared.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.507
- You should be.

00:11:11.507 --> 00:11:12.600
Because what I'm about to ask

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.350
is going to be quite difficult for you.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:16.853
Pull yourself together.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.970
That's it, that's all I'm asking.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.170
Get it together before it's too late.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.453
You're wasting your talent, your life.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.300
- I let you down.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:29.500
- [Lucifer] Then fix it.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:33.630
- Off Delilah, a glimmer
of hope in her eyes.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.610
Exterior Lux, street
night, Lucifer and Delilah

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:37.823
walk out saying goodbye.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.730
- Lucifer, I'm going to do what you asked.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:43.555
I am going to get it together.

00:11:43.555 --> 00:11:45.140
I promise.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.300
- Without me, all these terrible things

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:48.960
that weren't supposed to happen?

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.400
They happened.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.193
But what happens next is up to you.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.590
- She nods, smiles, pulls
him in an intense hug.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.930
They're still hugging
when a piece of shit car

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:00.990
slows to a stop in front of Lux.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:01.830
Shots ring out.

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:03.990
Lucifer and Delilah are
riddled with bullets.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.920
As they both go down in a
heap, the car screeches off.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:08.980
But without warning the shooter's car

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:11.280
is viciously broadsided by a city bus.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:12.880
A beat as everything settles.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.360
Then an unholy groan from Lucifer

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.960
as he rises to a sitting position.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.480
His clothes are torn with smoking holes.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.150
He rips his shirt open,
no blood, no entry wounds.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:25.082
Just pain, a lot of fucking pain.

00:12:25.082 --> 00:12:26.963
He slowly climbs to his feet,

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.790
goes over to Delilah,
beautiful in peaceful repose

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.321
and very much dead.

00:12:33.321 --> 00:12:35.780
Lucifer's face takes the pain.
- Very dead.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:36.730
- He looks down the street,

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:38.590
zeroes in to the wreckage
and stalks over to it.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:41.030
The shooter's body has been
thrown from the crumpled car

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.590
laid out in a pile of broken glass,

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.533
twisted and bloody, but still alive.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:47.030
- What did you do?

00:12:49.659 --> 00:12:50.540
- I'm sorry.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.070
- Sorry?

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.620
Tell me why.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.870
Why did you end her life?

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:58.759
I can smell death coming for you.

00:12:58.759 --> 00:13:00.682
Shall I speed it along?

00:13:00.682 --> 00:13:02.103
- Why else?

00:13:02.103 --> 00:13:02.936
Money.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:06.450
- Times like this I
wish I was back in hell.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.080
What I would do to you.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.573
- Hey, I just pulled the trigger.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.490
- [Lucifer] What do you mean by that?

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:18.790
- The shooter coughs up a
final geyser of blood and dies.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.530
Lucifer walks back over to Delilah,

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:21.760
he stands there staring down at her

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.420
with something in his eyes.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.840
Is it loss?

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.730
Which is when we realize
we're watching Lucifer

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:27.973
from someone else's POV.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.610
Exterior Lux, street.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.860
Find Amenadiel in the shadows,

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:34.700
a slow motion ballet of
onlookers around him.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.461
As he glares at Lucifer ominously,

00:13:36.461 --> 00:13:39.790
we wonder, did this actually
make it into the pilot?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.203
Is he observing this
moment or did he cause it?

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.340
Exterior, Lux street.
- We need Len here!

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:46.666
We need Len.

00:13:46.666 --> 00:13:49.000
- (laughing) same night.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:50.850
Now a full blown crime scene.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.620
Cherry tops spin, police swarm,

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.020
coroners put Delilah's body in a bag

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.440
and into the back of their van

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:58.500
as an unmarked cop car pulls up.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:03.219
Out hops LAPD homicide
detective Chloe Dancer.

00:14:03.219 --> 00:14:07.170
♪ Hold me closer, Chloe Dancer ♪

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:09.130
- Beautiful but downplays it on purpose.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:11.530
She's smart, cold, and direct.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.020
She's strides over to the red car

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:14.380
where the shooter still lies

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:16.460
in the bed of broken glass and blood,

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:17.293
bends over to get a closer look,

00:14:17.293 --> 00:14:19.500
when she hears some
snickering and whispering.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.893
Turns to see some rookie
uniform staring at her.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.073
- Can I help you?

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:28.860
- Nah, just talking about
some of our favorite movies.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.680
- Another plain clothes detective walks up

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:31.513
from the other direction.

00:14:31.513 --> 00:14:34.579
He's Daniel Espinoza, gruff, alpha dog.

00:14:34.579 --> 00:14:36.510
(everyone laughing)

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:39.263
- Hey, go secure the perimeter.

00:14:41.377 --> 00:14:43.010
- You here to babysit me?

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.320
Lieutenant said this is my case.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.190
- Well, hi.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.230
Nice to see you too.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.330
Yeah, it's your case Chloe.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.970
Want to hear what I got so far though?

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:55.550
- No.

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:57.380
- Well, it's an easy one.

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:00.620
(laughing) This is our
bad guy, Eddie Deakin.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.410
Low-level drug dealer.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:04.600
Found these in his pocket

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.653
and this in Delilah's purse.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:13.370
So obviously drug related, right?

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:16.470
Maybe she owed him a bunch
of cash or something.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.523
She wasn't exactly selling
out stadiums these days.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.550
- But how'd you know he's low level?

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:24.920
- Do you see his car?

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:25.753
- Yeah, but look.

00:15:25.753 --> 00:15:27.010
Look at his watch.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:28.470
That ain't cheap.

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:29.970
- Probably a fake.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.800
Wouldn't pick too hard at this one, Chloe.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:36.100
Not after Palmetto street.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.573
- Ah, Palmetto street!
(everyone laughing)

00:15:39.573 --> 00:15:40.490
- Palmetto!

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:41.790
- Woo!

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:42.790
- Listen, Dan.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:46.010
I begged for this case
because of Palmetto.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.623
So any witnesses?

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:49.780
- Interior Lux, night,

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:51.820
where Chloe is now questioning Lucifer.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:52.790
He's distracted.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:55.350
His rolling emotions over Delilah's death

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.810
are disorienting him.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.090
Maze hovers nearby

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:03.140
- Lucifer Morningstar, is that like

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.150
a stage name or something?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.497
- God given, I'm afraid.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.803
You look familiar, have we met?

00:16:11.218 --> 00:16:13.160
- Yeah, five minutes ago.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.736
And I'm asking the questions.

00:16:14.736 --> 00:16:17.077
Talk to me about your
relationship with the victim.

00:16:17.077 --> 00:16:19.990
- She used to work here a few years back.

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:23.390
I would occasionally
accompany her while she sang.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:24.520
Then she became a big star

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:26.320
and someone decided to end her life.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.700
- Did you know the shooter?

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.470
- [Lucifer] No, but we did
have a nice little chat.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:32.770
I asked him why he did it.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.343
- I see.

00:16:35.343 --> 00:16:36.693
You like to play cop, do you?

00:16:36.693 --> 00:16:38.420
- I like to play in general, Detective.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:39.717
What about you?

00:16:39.717 --> 00:16:41.640
(Dan chuckling)

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.650
- It's interesting because
the coroner's report

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:45.460
has the shooter killed on impact.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.590
So you spoke to a dead guy?

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.120
- Well, he wasn't quite dead.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.923
His soul was still crossing the threshold.

00:16:51.923 --> 00:16:54.323
- Oh, okay then.

00:16:54.323 --> 00:16:55.690
So why'd he do it?

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:57.440
- Well, money of course.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.224
You humans love your money.

00:16:59.224 --> 00:17:00.400
- Yes.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.233
Yes we do.

00:17:01.233 --> 00:17:03.364
And what planet are you from, London?

00:17:03.364 --> 00:17:07.700
- (chuckling) He also said
"I just pulled the trigger."

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:08.673
Interesting, no?

00:17:10.313 --> 00:17:12.950
- Delilah was shot to
death by a drug dealer

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:15.610
and looks like Delilah herself
kept the guy pretty busy.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:18.070
It's sad, it's ugly, but
it's not rocket science.

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.350
I mean, something obviously
went south between them.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:21.590
She gets riddled with bullets

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:23.623
and a nice little act
of God takes him out.

00:17:23.623 --> 00:17:25.563
- It doesn't work like that.

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:28.460
Quite neatly wrapped present for the LAPD,

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.537
don't you think?

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:31.750
- Okay.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.300
How does she end up dying
in a hailstorm of bullets

00:17:35.738 --> 00:17:38.280
and you get away without a scratch?

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.350
That's very interesting, don't you think?

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:42.320
- [Lucifer] The benefits of immortality?

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.670
- Immortality, yes, of course.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.910
Do you spell that with one M or two?

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:48.520
I always forget.

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:51.630
- What will your corrupt little
organization do about this?

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:52.960
- [Chloe] Excuse me?

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.280
- Will you find the one responsible?

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.630
Will he be punished?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.363
Will this be a priority for you?

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.520
- You've got some balls on you, you know.

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:01.508
- [Lucifer] Well thank you very much,

00:18:01.508 --> 00:18:02.642
but they're really quite average.

00:18:02.642 --> 00:18:05.237
- I knew that.

00:18:05.237 --> 00:18:07.390
- Are you sure that we haven't met?

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.630
I could swear I've seen you naked.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:10.703
Did we have sex?

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.570
- You know what, go to hell.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.980
- No thank you, much more fun here.

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:18.170
Oh wait detective, we're not done.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.850
- Yes, we are.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:20.683
- And she's out.

00:18:20.683 --> 00:18:22.260
Off Lucifer frustrated.

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:24.363
We end act one.

00:18:24.363 --> 00:18:27.270
- Meet cute, that was the meet cute.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:28.103
- Yay!

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:31.220
I don't think those two
are ever going to hook up.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.770
- Never.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.320
- Act two.

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.360
Interior Lux, later that night.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.460
Lucifer plays piano.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:42.110
Fingers flying, an intense
version of Bowie's Lady Stardust.

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:44.860
Suddenly he smashes the keys
in a burst of atonal fury,

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.810
his gaze fixed on something ahead.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.970
It's his reflection in
the mirrored fireplace,

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.470
that disturbing face again.

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:52.430
We catch just a hint of it before

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:54.290
he gets up at hurls a
metal skull at the mirror,

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.900
smashing it to pieces.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:58.410
Maze enters, surveys
the damage, says nothing

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:01.330
which only serves to
infuriate Lucifer even more

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:03.110
and really make the audience curious.

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:04.463
Did we see this scene?

00:19:04.463 --> 00:19:07.463
- (laughing) Out with it, Maze.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.093
- I'm curious.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.740
- [Lucifer] About?

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:14.640
- Why this upsets you so much.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.410
- 'Cause there is someone out there

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:20.325
that deserves punishment and
it's not going to happen.

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:21.570
- Who cares?

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.090
Mortals die every day.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.720
- Yes, insignificant ones.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.560
Human nothings never add
anything to this world.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.800
They only take and consume

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:34.170
and die cowardly, pathetic
deaths, but this was different.

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:35.343
She was different.

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.530
- You care about her.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:40.970
- Please.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:43.810
I care about punishing
the coward responsible.

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:45.010
- Who are you right now?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.140
- I don't mind the occasional
smart ass remarks, Maze.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:52.830
They can be amusing,
but don't disrespect me.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.410
- The opposite is true.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:57.910
You're the Prince of freaking darkness.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.730
It's all well and good to take a vacation,

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:02.910
have fun in paradise with
all the low hanging fruit.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:06.700
But you're losing sight of
who you actually are, Lucifer.

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:10.550
You exist to punish and
torture for a universal reason.

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:14.147
Certainly not for a petty
human emotion, such as love.

00:20:14.147 --> 00:20:17.550
- (chuckling) I am not human.

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:18.383
Take that back.

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:21.670
The world was robbed of a great talent

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.240
and that makes me angry.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.820
It makes me want to punish someone

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.913
in very unholy ways, that's all.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:31.640
- Does that mean we're going home?

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:32.700
- He's silent.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.250
Her smile fades, but
she kisses him sensually

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:36.140
then slinks off.

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:38.450
On Lucifer.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:39.500
Maze's words echoing.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.530
- We did shoot that scene,

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.770
but it never made it.
- We did shoot that scene.

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:43.683
- Deleted scenes.

00:20:44.806 --> 00:20:47.160
Exterior, Malibu coastline.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.611
- Too blue for Fox, that one.

00:20:48.611 --> 00:20:51.470
(everyone laughing)

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:52.870
- Gliding over the beautiful ocean side.

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.280
We pick up Lucifer's Jag

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:56.020
as it speeds down the ribbon of highway

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.770
that is the PCH.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.090
Exterior Malibu wedding site, day.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:01.300
The wedding is in progress.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:04.310
A short sweaty music
mogul named Jimmy Barnes

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:07.960
is about to wed a stunning
statuesque supermodel bride.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.970
Surrounded by family and frenemies,

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:11.480
it's a whole big to-do.

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:14.900
The priest has just arrived
at the part where he says,

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:17.771
- Speak now or forever hold your peace.

00:21:17.771 --> 00:21:19.027
- Yeah, excuse me!

00:21:19.027 --> 00:21:21.210
- And Lucifer comes
strolling down that aisle.

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.990
- I have a problem.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:25.270
Has anyone else noticed how incredibly

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:27.820
jaw-droppingly, loin-stirringly beautiful

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:29.270
this young woman is,

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:32.080
and how short, sweaty and altogether fugly

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:33.620
this homunculus is?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:35.429
I mean, what is this, a
wedding or a kidnapping?

00:21:35.429 --> 00:21:36.457
You know what I mean?

00:21:36.457 --> 00:21:38.251
(everyone chuckling)

00:21:38.251 --> 00:21:39.900
- The priest crosses himself.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:41.270
- Yeah, good luck with that, Padre.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:44.310
Oh, while you're at it tell him
I say hey, it's been awhile.

00:21:44.310 --> 00:21:46.420
Jimmy Barnes!

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.253
Remember me?

00:21:48.309 --> 00:21:52.610
- Hey man, this is a private event.

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:53.920
How'd you even get in here?

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:55.028
- Yes, quite a lavish

00:21:55.028 --> 00:21:58.900
be it tacky one for a
record producer on the outs.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:00.033
Do you remember me?

00:22:01.449 --> 00:22:04.420
- Of course I remember you.

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:05.529
What do you want?

00:22:05.529 --> 00:22:06.362
I'm a little busy.

00:22:06.362 --> 00:22:08.250
- I can't believe you're getting married

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:09.710
the day after your ex-lover

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:12.613
and once brightest star
was murdered in cold blood.

00:22:14.048 --> 00:22:15.510
- Yeah.

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:20.510
It's sad, but Delilah ruined
my wedding once before.

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:22.800
I wasn't about to let her do it again.

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:23.920
- Yes.

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:25.920
It was hard to be
rejected, isn't it, Jimmy?

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:26.753
Twice.

00:22:28.050 --> 00:22:29.215
- What?

00:22:29.215 --> 00:22:30.048
She said you tried.

00:22:30.048 --> 00:22:32.700
She said you tried to
get her back recently.

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:34.890
I'd killed someone if they denied me once.

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.810
Not that that's possible, come on.

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:38.820
Come on, tell me Jimbo.

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:40.680
Did you want her dead?

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:42.503
You know I love a juicy story.

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:48.670
- I am not playing that
mind game with you.

00:22:48.670 --> 00:22:49.580
Of course not.

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:53.040
I was furious and humiliated
when she dumped me.

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:56.579
But I think I rebound pretty well.

00:22:56.579 --> 00:22:58.533
- Clearly, respect.

00:23:00.590 --> 00:23:03.233
- You should go play
your games with 2Vile.

00:23:04.510 --> 00:23:06.110
- 2Vile, the rapper?

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:07.013
- Yeah, mhmm.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:10.370
Delilah dumped me for that lunatic.

00:23:10.370 --> 00:23:12.830
A, they were always fighting.

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:15.320
I think he slapped her around a bunch.

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:16.620
He's the real deal, man.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:18.680
And he's surrounded by a bunch

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:22.620
of gun-toting morons 24/7.

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.810
- Oh, I'm sorry, how rude of me.

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:26.423
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:30.203
- I really don't want to
have sex with him tonight.

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:32.739
I'm sorry, did I just say?

00:23:32.739 --> 00:23:34.853
I didn't mean that.

00:23:34.853 --> 00:23:35.900
- Of course you're don't.

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:36.750
Let's be honest here.

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:38.240
You're not marrying this human stain

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:40.323
because you're actually
in love with him, right?

00:23:41.646 --> 00:23:45.073
- No, I guess it's more about lifestyle.

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:47.780
I don't know what I was thinking

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:50.170
- Well good luck with that, he's broke.

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:51.660
Dry your tears, darling.

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.980
At least you'll have this magical day.

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:55.930
Well, I should be going.

00:23:55.930 --> 00:23:58.558
Best of luck to you crazy kids.

00:23:58.558 --> 00:24:00.680
- Lucifer turns and
walks off down the aisle,

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:03.715
a figurative mushroom cloud in his wake.

00:24:03.715 --> 00:24:05.927
(actors laughing)

00:24:05.927 --> 00:24:08.650
Exterior 2Vile's place,
Hollywood Hills, day.

00:24:08.650 --> 00:24:12.170
Lucifer cruises at the
drive of a pimped out palace

00:24:12.170 --> 00:24:14.670
that could easily have its
own very special episode

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:16.320
of MTV cribs.

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:18.360
Lucifer exits his car, rings the bell,

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:20.040
a massive gong sounds.

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:22.660
Door's opened by a white English butler.

00:24:22.660 --> 00:24:23.760
- Good afternoon, sir.

00:24:24.776 --> 00:24:27.779
- I'm here to see the
man sadly known as 2Vile.

00:24:27.779 --> 00:24:28.840
Is he in?

00:24:28.840 --> 00:24:30.260
- I'm sorry, sir.

00:24:30.260 --> 00:24:31.850
He's unavailable.

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:33.593
I'm afraid he's in the mourning.

00:24:33.593 --> 00:24:36.020
- I have narcotics for him.

00:24:36.020 --> 00:24:37.451
- Right this way, sir.

00:24:37.451 --> 00:24:39.073
- Okay.

00:24:39.073 --> 00:24:41.590
- Inside 2Vile's place moments later,

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:43.420
Lucifer follows the Butler into the den,

00:24:43.420 --> 00:24:45.340
furniture from MoMA.

00:24:45.340 --> 00:24:47.930
2Vile's crews are scattered
all over the place.

00:24:47.930 --> 00:24:49.050
Hip-hop's thumping.

00:24:49.050 --> 00:24:51.940
There's tons of weed,
weapons, it's a real scene.

00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:54.460
An immensely expensive
plasma TV in the background

00:24:54.460 --> 00:24:56.340
plays news on Delilah's death.

00:24:56.340 --> 00:24:57.420
The hot headline.

00:24:57.420 --> 00:25:01.840
- Can someone please turn
down this God awful music?

00:25:01.840 --> 00:25:02.993
- Who's this clown?

00:25:06.580 --> 00:25:09.513
- Oh, he has narcotics for you, sir.

00:25:09.513 --> 00:25:11.773
- The name is Lucifer Morningstar.

00:25:13.510 --> 00:25:15.720
- Lucifer Morningstar?

00:25:15.720 --> 00:25:17.200
That's a good hip hop name.

00:25:17.200 --> 00:25:18.886
- That offends me.

00:25:18.886 --> 00:25:19.719
- What do you,

00:25:19.719 --> 00:25:21.460
what, you don't like hip hop?

00:25:21.460 --> 00:25:23.710
- No, I most certainly do not.

00:25:23.710 --> 00:25:25.550
- Well that offends me.

00:25:25.550 --> 00:25:27.540
You have a problem with black people?

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:28.580
- Not in the slightest.

00:25:28.580 --> 00:25:29.930
I just hate your music.

00:25:29.930 --> 00:25:32.700
When I say your music, I mean your music.

00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:34.410
Not music made by other black people.

00:25:34.410 --> 00:25:37.220
Without the blues, there'll be
no devil's music whatsoever.

00:25:37.220 --> 00:25:39.380
There are of course many
giants in the field.

00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:40.760
Just not you.

00:25:40.760 --> 00:25:41.623
Am I being clear?

00:25:42.750 --> 00:25:44.420
- You're being clear, all right,

00:25:44.420 --> 00:25:45.820
If you're looking to get yourself killed.

00:25:45.820 --> 00:25:48.490
- Don't waste your
munitions, I'm immortal.

00:25:48.490 --> 00:25:49.763
Tell me about Delilah.

00:25:50.750 --> 00:25:51.970
- What's to tell?

00:25:51.970 --> 00:25:53.380
Bitch is dead.

00:25:53.380 --> 00:25:54.440
- That ignites Lucifer.

00:25:54.440 --> 00:25:56.220
He violently shoves 2Vile,

00:25:56.220 --> 00:25:57.980
sending him shattering
through a glass door,

00:25:57.980 --> 00:26:00.510
toppling over the
balcony to certain death.

00:26:00.510 --> 00:26:03.430
Just as Lucifer grabs him
by his blinged out chains,

00:26:03.430 --> 00:26:05.430
suspending him high above the hillside.

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:07.210
- No, no, no, no, don't shoot him.

00:26:07.210 --> 00:26:08.560
Don't shoot him, you idiot.

00:26:10.310 --> 00:26:11.393
I didn't kill her!

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:13.680
- Why should I believe you?

00:26:13.680 --> 00:26:14.960
- Because I loved her.

00:26:14.960 --> 00:26:16.920
- People sometimes kill people
with whom they're in love.

00:26:16.920 --> 00:26:18.870
The heart is mysterious or so I'm told.

00:26:20.160 --> 00:26:22.030
- Girl made me crazy, okay.

00:26:22.030 --> 00:26:23.260
- Well women can do that.

00:26:23.260 --> 00:26:24.980
Doesn't mean you should beat her up.

00:26:24.980 --> 00:26:26.820
- Hey, hey, hey, come on.

00:26:26.820 --> 00:26:28.440
We worked that out a long time ago.

00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:29.360
I hit her once.

00:26:29.360 --> 00:26:31.453
'Cause she was cheating on me.

00:26:32.970 --> 00:26:33.920
- Huh.

00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:35.341
With whom?

00:26:35.341 --> 00:26:36.410
- I don't know.

00:26:36.410 --> 00:26:38.810
She wouldn't tell me,
said it was a big secret.

00:26:38.810 --> 00:26:40.740
Some rich married guy.

00:26:40.740 --> 00:26:44.040
- Well did she have a friend
she might've confided in?

00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:45.490
- Didn't trust no one.

00:26:45.490 --> 00:26:48.000
Her therapist is probably
the only one who knows.

00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:49.713
Some doc.

00:26:49.713 --> 00:26:52.300
(tune playing)

00:26:52.300 --> 00:26:54.067
Sorry about that.

00:26:54.067 --> 00:26:57.680
Some Dr. Linda in Beverly Hills.

00:26:57.680 --> 00:26:59.153
- That's Dr. Linda's music.

00:26:59.153 --> 00:27:00.450
- Yeah.

00:27:00.450 --> 00:27:03.587
Saw her like five times a week on the DL.

00:27:04.620 --> 00:27:06.830
Used a fake name and everything.

00:27:06.830 --> 00:27:09.503
- Thank you for your time. (sighing)

00:27:10.590 --> 00:27:13.930
- Man, sometimes I get
tired of fronting, you know?

00:27:13.930 --> 00:27:16.120
I really just wanted to
put a ring on that finger

00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:17.883
and a baby up in there.

00:27:17.883 --> 00:27:19.350
(everyone chuckling)

00:27:19.350 --> 00:27:21.590
Wow, she was the one.

00:27:21.590 --> 00:27:23.508
Now she's dead.

00:27:23.508 --> 00:27:24.730
- You know, I like the side of you.

00:27:24.730 --> 00:27:26.350
You might consider putting
this kind of emotion

00:27:26.350 --> 00:27:27.650
into your music.

00:27:27.650 --> 00:27:29.350
And change your name.

00:27:29.350 --> 00:27:31.530
What does your mother call you?

00:27:31.530 --> 00:27:33.060
- Percy.

00:27:33.060 --> 00:27:33.943
Percy Wallace.

00:27:35.460 --> 00:27:36.580
- Yeah, nevermind.

00:27:36.580 --> 00:27:39.630
Good luck with what's left
of your short lived career.

00:27:39.630 --> 00:27:42.230
- Lucifer starts to leave when,

00:27:42.230 --> 00:27:43.693
- Guns down, on the floor!

00:27:44.920 --> 00:27:46.570
- Detective!

00:27:46.570 --> 00:27:48.420
Welcome to the party.

00:27:48.420 --> 00:27:50.410
- Guns down.

00:27:50.410 --> 00:27:52.090
You, grab that bucket.

00:27:52.090 --> 00:27:53.360
Pick them up now.

00:27:53.360 --> 00:27:54.530
- Oh, you sly dog.

00:27:54.530 --> 00:27:56.540
You did listen to me.

00:27:56.540 --> 00:27:58.280
- Ran the dead guy's cell phone.

00:27:58.280 --> 00:28:00.080
2Vile was the last person he called.

00:28:03.540 --> 00:28:05.230
Oh, come on, man!
- Oh, sorry!

00:28:05.230 --> 00:28:06.080
Oh, come on, man!

00:28:07.250 --> 00:28:09.430
- What I find highly interesting

00:28:09.430 --> 00:28:11.930
is how you made the
connection on your own.

00:28:11.930 --> 00:28:13.480
- Well I've been busy, my dear.

00:28:14.550 --> 00:28:15.910
- Talk to me about Delilah.

00:28:15.910 --> 00:28:18.400
- Yes, yes, we've been
over that one, detective.

00:28:18.400 --> 00:28:20.530
- And why you called the shooter two days

00:28:20.530 --> 00:28:21.910
before she was murdered.

00:28:21.910 --> 00:28:23.100
- Fine, yeah, yeah.

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:26.720
I called Eddie cause he
hooks me up sometimes.

00:28:26.720 --> 00:28:28.810
He met Delilah through me.

00:28:28.810 --> 00:28:30.120
When we were together, whatever.

00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:32.740
Don't don't make me a killer, do it?

00:28:32.740 --> 00:28:35.060
- No, but it does make you a suspect.

00:28:35.060 --> 00:28:38.470
- What, so everyone on
Eddie's phone is a suspect?

00:28:38.470 --> 00:28:39.740
You joking?

00:28:39.740 --> 00:28:42.550
Welcome to the celebrity name game.

00:28:42.550 --> 00:28:45.600
You're going to drag half
of Hollywood downtown?

00:28:45.600 --> 00:28:46.803
Be like the Oscars.

00:28:49.210 --> 00:28:51.070
- Chloe reaches for her cuffs.

00:28:51.070 --> 00:28:53.790
Meanwhile, the celebrity moment
has triggered recognition

00:28:53.790 --> 00:28:55.363
in one of 2Vile's crew.

00:28:57.250 --> 00:28:58.633
- Dennis, you're muted.

00:29:03.744 --> 00:29:05.617
- I knew that was gonna happen.

00:29:07.750 --> 00:29:09.820
Wait, wait, wait.

00:29:09.820 --> 00:29:11.620
Aren't you that chick from the film?

00:29:12.600 --> 00:29:13.850
- What's this, what film?

00:29:15.230 --> 00:29:17.663
- Yeah you used to be
that actress or something.

00:29:18.920 --> 00:29:20.070
Right?

00:29:20.070 --> 00:29:22.058
I mean that teen movie.

00:29:22.058 --> 00:29:24.400
I forget what it's called.

00:29:24.400 --> 00:29:26.490
- Of course!

00:29:26.490 --> 00:29:29.330
Hot Tub High School, that's
where I know you from!

00:29:29.330 --> 00:29:31.910
- Let's stick to my questions
shall we, thank you.

00:29:31.910 --> 00:29:34.180
- The one with the famous nude
scene coming out the hot tub.

00:29:34.180 --> 00:29:35.470
It was a complete Fast Times ripoff.

00:29:35.470 --> 00:29:36.880
You were like the new Phoebe Cates.

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:38.870
Oh, that was quite a nude scene.

00:29:38.870 --> 00:29:40.500
- I've got way too many bullets in here

00:29:40.500 --> 00:29:42.140
for you still to be talking.

00:29:42.140 --> 00:29:43.968
Come on, you're under arrest.

00:29:43.968 --> 00:29:45.120
- That's a waste of time, detective.

00:29:45.120 --> 00:29:46.110
I've just threatened his life.

00:29:46.110 --> 00:29:46.943
He's not our guy.

00:29:46.943 --> 00:29:48.290
He would have said, trust me.

00:29:49.300 --> 00:29:50.433
- What, you did what?

00:29:51.740 --> 00:29:53.333
- Yeah, isn't that illegal?

00:29:54.700 --> 00:29:57.580
- A little bit, yeah.

00:29:57.580 --> 00:29:59.300
Okay, you don't go anywhere.

00:29:59.300 --> 00:30:00.770
You come with me.

00:30:00.770 --> 00:30:02.503
- Oh, with pleasure.

00:30:03.470 --> 00:30:05.980
Do these go any tighter, Detective?

00:30:05.980 --> 00:30:07.730
- Chloe slaps the cuffs on Lucifer

00:30:07.730 --> 00:30:09.700
and a smug smile doesn't leave his lips

00:30:09.700 --> 00:30:11.800
as Chloe yanks him out.

00:30:11.800 --> 00:30:13.190
Exterior 2Vile's place.

00:30:13.190 --> 00:30:15.300
You know, we think it'd be really fun

00:30:15.300 --> 00:30:17.593
if we just did a little thing right here.

00:30:18.730 --> 00:30:20.800
Lucifer and Chloe,

00:30:20.800 --> 00:30:22.120
why don't you switch?

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:24.773
Or Tom and Lauren, switch roles?

00:30:24.773 --> 00:30:25.606
- Yes.

00:30:25.606 --> 00:30:27.040
- Oh yes.
- Just switch roles?

00:30:27.040 --> 00:30:27.950
Okay.

00:30:27.950 --> 00:30:28.783
- Are you ready?

00:30:28.783 --> 00:30:30.066
- Yeah.
- In unit?

00:30:30.066 --> 00:30:30.899
- Okay.

00:30:33.444 --> 00:30:34.460
All right.

00:30:34.460 --> 00:30:36.320
At least perhaps you'll listen to me

00:30:36.320 --> 00:30:38.740
although not sure I understand
why I'm being arrested.

00:30:38.740 --> 00:30:43.200
- 'Cause you're interfering
with a police investigation?

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:45.430
You've broken I can't
even count how many laws

00:30:45.430 --> 00:30:47.083
and you piss me off.

00:30:48.470 --> 00:30:50.000
- Don't like that.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:51.700
- I can get out of these, you know.

00:30:51.700 --> 00:30:52.833
- Funny.

00:30:52.833 --> 00:30:55.260
What, how did you do that?

00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:56.660
You a magician or something?

00:30:57.510 --> 00:30:58.847
- You're still wasting time.

00:30:58.847 --> 00:31:01.390
We should be out there solving a homicide

00:31:01.390 --> 00:31:03.860
and punishing those responsible!

00:31:03.860 --> 00:31:04.920
- We?

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:05.810
Are you insane?

00:31:05.810 --> 00:31:07.910
Get in the car, I'm taking you in.

00:31:07.910 --> 00:31:09.360
- But that's boring,

00:31:09.360 --> 00:31:10.880
not to mention pointless.

00:31:10.880 --> 00:31:12.440
Come on, it'll be fun!

00:31:13.837 --> 00:31:15.960
- How could you possibly help me?

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:18.500
- Mm-mm, you'd be surprised detective.

00:31:18.500 --> 00:31:20.480
I have a certain skillset, mmm.

00:31:20.480 --> 00:31:22.870
I can be very persuasive with people,

00:31:22.870 --> 00:31:25.420
I tend to see things others can not.

00:31:25.420 --> 00:31:26.520
- So you're a psychic.

00:31:27.610 --> 00:31:29.720
- No, no, I can't read people's minds.

00:31:29.720 --> 00:31:30.553
I'm not a Jedi.

00:31:31.556 --> 00:31:33.389
People tell me things.

00:31:34.430 --> 00:31:37.230
- Really, just confess their sins?

00:31:37.230 --> 00:31:38.910
Just like that?

00:31:38.910 --> 00:31:39.960
- No.

00:31:39.960 --> 00:31:42.660
Not their sins, I have no
power over people's sins,

00:31:42.660 --> 00:31:44.040
I actually get a bad rap to that.

00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:47.310
But their desires, mm,
different thing entirely.

00:31:47.310 --> 00:31:50.280
I have the ability to draw out
people's forbidden desires,

00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:51.760
tempt them, taunt them.

00:31:51.760 --> 00:31:54.490
The more simple, more
human, the easier it is.

00:31:54.490 --> 00:31:57.820
The more complex, the more
challenging and exciting really.

00:31:57.820 --> 00:32:01.510
But your actual sins, the
sins are on you people.

00:32:01.510 --> 00:32:03.773
- Are you in Bridgerton?

00:32:03.773 --> 00:32:06.667
(everyone laughing)

00:32:06.667 --> 00:32:08.860
- Season two, season two!

00:32:08.860 --> 00:32:09.870
- You people.

00:32:09.870 --> 00:32:11.890
I get it, the name, the
whole Lucifer thing.

00:32:11.890 --> 00:32:14.797
And what, desire is like your super power?

00:32:14.797 --> 00:32:16.663
- More like a gift from God.

00:32:17.670 --> 00:32:19.030
Look, I'm just a people person.

00:32:19.030 --> 00:32:20.660
They feel compelled to
share things with me.

00:32:20.660 --> 00:32:22.610
And why wouldn't they really?

00:32:22.610 --> 00:32:24.110
I'm pretty awesome.

00:32:24.110 --> 00:32:26.460
- Yeah? Prove it.

00:32:26.460 --> 00:32:27.293
- That I'm awesome?

00:32:27.293 --> 00:32:28.990
Isn't it obvious?

00:32:28.990 --> 00:32:30.580
Tell me detective,

00:32:30.580 --> 00:32:34.703
what do you desire more than
anything else in this life?

00:32:38.550 --> 00:32:40.140
- When I was a little girl

00:32:40.140 --> 00:32:42.650
I always wanted to be a cop like my daddy

00:32:42.650 --> 00:32:46.950
so that one day I could help
people make a difference

00:32:46.950 --> 00:32:49.793
and make them shut up
and get in the damn car.

00:32:51.790 --> 00:32:54.700
- You're not like a Jedi
or something are you?

00:32:54.700 --> 00:32:56.990
- Get in the car.

00:32:56.990 --> 00:32:58.950
- Wait, I know something you don't know.

00:32:58.950 --> 00:33:00.380
- [Chloe] Yeah, what's that?

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:02.390
- Won't say unless you
