00:43:00.018 --> 00:43:01.310
Watch and learn.

00:43:01.310 --> 00:43:03.563
Linda, darling, tell me.

00:43:04.940 --> 00:43:07.829
- No, I can't. (giggling)

00:43:07.829 --> 00:43:11.123
I want to, you know, but I can't.

00:43:12.795 --> 00:43:14.206
You're the devil!

00:43:14.206 --> 00:43:15.490
- (chuckling) Correct.

00:43:15.490 --> 00:43:18.709
Now tell me, Dr. Martin,
'cause I know you want to.

00:43:18.709 --> 00:43:19.626
- Oh, darn!

00:43:22.323 --> 00:43:24.973
And it's really juicy too!

00:43:28.066 --> 00:43:30.200
- Did you roofie her?

00:43:30.200 --> 00:43:31.460
This is unbelievable.

00:43:31.460 --> 00:43:32.310
- That's not her fault.

00:43:32.310 --> 00:43:33.980
She's just reacting to me.

00:43:33.980 --> 00:43:35.090
Watch and learn.

00:43:35.090 --> 00:43:36.920
The answer is yes, Linda.

00:43:36.920 --> 00:43:38.613
We can take a trip to
pound town if we must

00:43:38.613 --> 00:43:40.643
but you have to tell us.

00:43:40.643 --> 00:43:45.643
- Mmmm (chuckling) okay!

00:43:46.633 --> 00:43:48.067
It's Grey Cooper.

00:43:49.211 --> 00:43:50.403
- What?!

00:43:50.403 --> 00:43:52.030
Grey Cooper?

00:43:52.030 --> 00:43:54.124
That is pretty juicy.

00:43:54.124 --> 00:43:55.140
- The actor?

00:43:55.140 --> 00:43:56.640
The one married to Amanda what's her face?

00:43:56.640 --> 00:43:58.150
Oh he's horrible.

00:43:58.150 --> 00:44:00.733
So square jawed and handsome, so vanilla.

00:44:01.710 --> 00:44:03.040
Quite disappointed in Delilah.

00:44:03.040 --> 00:44:05.113
Truly terrible taste in the opposite sex.

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:07.810
- Thank you, Doctor.

00:44:07.810 --> 00:44:09.884
We will definitely be in touch.

00:44:09.884 --> 00:44:11.541
Lucifer, let's go.

00:44:11.541 --> 00:44:12.547
- Of course, but I made a deal.

00:44:12.547 --> 00:44:15.529
I need to hold up my end of the bargain.

00:44:15.529 --> 00:44:17.270
- What, you're not actually talking

00:44:17.270 --> 00:44:19.713
about having sex with
her right now, are you?

00:44:23.160 --> 00:44:24.743
- I do a lot of yoga.

00:44:25.791 --> 00:44:26.624
Hot yoga.

00:44:28.790 --> 00:44:31.623
I'm freakishly flexible.

00:44:31.623 --> 00:44:32.456
See?

00:44:33.610 --> 00:44:36.166
Wow, really tried to keep that in.

00:44:36.166 --> 00:44:38.260
- You tried, that's what matters.

00:44:38.260 --> 00:44:40.880
I do apologize, but I'm going
to have to take a rain check.

00:44:40.880 --> 00:44:41.753
I will be back.

00:44:43.140 --> 00:44:44.502
- I certainly hope so.

00:44:44.502 --> 00:44:47.077
- My word is my bond.

00:44:47.077 --> 00:44:49.781
- Chloe's shaking her head.

00:44:49.781 --> 00:44:51.670
She's beyond stymied.

00:44:51.670 --> 00:44:53.530
Following Lucifer out.

00:44:53.530 --> 00:44:56.150
Exterior, downtown industrial area.

00:44:56.150 --> 00:44:58.990
Lucifer walks with purpose
down a dingy street

00:44:58.990 --> 00:45:01.430
pushing his way past a group of onlookers

00:45:01.430 --> 00:45:03.100
crowded behind a barrier.

00:45:03.100 --> 00:45:04.120
As he starts to pass,

00:45:04.120 --> 00:45:07.250
a feeble traffic cop tries to stop him.

00:45:07.250 --> 00:45:08.083
- Sir?

00:45:08.083 --> 00:45:11.070
Sir, you have to stay
behind the barricade.

00:45:11.070 --> 00:45:13.850
- Lucifer ignores him, stepping
casually past the barricade

00:45:13.850 --> 00:45:16.270
when suddenly a muscle car
comes speeding around the corner

00:45:16.270 --> 00:45:17.930
pursued by two police cars.

00:45:17.930 --> 00:45:20.510
Lights, sirens and gunfire.

00:45:20.510 --> 00:45:22.400
Muscle car's tire blows

00:45:22.400 --> 00:45:26.290
and the car flips and crash
slides right toward Lucifer

00:45:26.290 --> 00:45:29.180
who doesn't move as it skids
to a halt inches from him,

00:45:29.180 --> 00:45:30.624
when we hear,

00:45:30.624 --> 00:45:33.363
- Who the fuck is this guy?

00:45:34.760 --> 00:45:36.943
- Oh, he's with me, sorry.

00:45:38.370 --> 00:45:41.960
- But you're not Grey Cooper.

00:45:41.960 --> 00:45:43.500
- No, of course not.

00:45:43.500 --> 00:45:44.833
What the hell is this?

00:45:45.698 --> 00:45:47.653
- We need to speak with Grey Cooper.

00:45:48.970 --> 00:45:51.790
- Exterior downtown street,
different area moments later.

00:45:51.790 --> 00:45:54.600
Lucifer and Chloe now
with the real Grey Cooper,

00:45:54.600 --> 00:45:57.080
same cuts and bruises as a stunt guy

00:45:57.080 --> 00:45:58.530
and the uniform stand nearby.

00:46:00.134 --> 00:46:02.800
- Oh, Delilah, yeah.

00:46:02.800 --> 00:46:04.880
I heard about that this morning.

00:46:04.880 --> 00:46:06.430
Can't believe it.

00:46:06.430 --> 00:46:08.680
We did a movie together last year.

00:46:08.680 --> 00:46:10.400
Got pretty close.

00:46:10.400 --> 00:46:11.880
- Lovers?

00:46:11.880 --> 00:46:12.890
- Friends.

00:46:12.890 --> 00:46:14.750
- Friends who were lovers.

00:46:14.750 --> 00:46:15.583
- Settle down.

00:46:15.583 --> 00:46:16.906
I'll handle the questions, thank you.

00:46:16.906 --> 00:46:19.820
Mr. Cooper, when did you last
have contact with Delilah?

00:46:19.820 --> 00:46:21.200
- Sorry, I just have one more question

00:46:21.200 --> 00:46:23.790
before we proceed with the boring ones.

00:46:23.790 --> 00:46:26.480
Mr. Cooper, what do you
want more than anything?

00:46:26.480 --> 00:46:27.313
What is it?

00:46:27.313 --> 00:46:29.610
What's your deepest, darkest desire?

00:46:29.610 --> 00:46:31.560
When you close your eyes, what do you see?

00:46:31.560 --> 00:46:34.968
- I'm the president of the United States.

00:46:34.968 --> 00:46:35.980
- Hah!

00:46:35.980 --> 00:46:37.680
Who's the devil now?

00:46:37.680 --> 00:46:40.705
- Those are some pretty big
aspirations there, Mr. Cooper.

00:46:40.705 --> 00:46:43.439
- Well, after the acting and stuff.

00:46:43.439 --> 00:46:45.220
- Oh, don't be embarrassed.

00:46:45.220 --> 00:46:46.670
Hell if Arnold can do it, right?

00:46:46.670 --> 00:46:48.730
But you wouldn't want any nasty secrets

00:46:48.730 --> 00:46:50.533
screwing that up for you, would you?

00:46:50.533 --> 00:46:51.883
- No, no, no, I wouldn't.

00:46:52.780 --> 00:46:55.320
- Better to pull the skeletons out now,

00:46:55.320 --> 00:46:57.010
the public's very forgetful.

00:46:57.010 --> 00:46:59.310
- More importantly, why would
you want to be a politician?

00:46:59.310 --> 00:47:01.010
I mean, you get to make movies,

00:47:01.010 --> 00:47:02.440
isn't that much more fun?

00:47:02.440 --> 00:47:03.913
Not that I like yours much.

00:47:05.060 --> 00:47:06.653
- Is there a point to this?

00:47:07.970 --> 00:47:10.620
- Mr. Cooper, were you having
an affair with Delilah?

00:47:11.570 --> 00:47:14.020
- Honey, have you been getting my texts?

00:47:14.020 --> 00:47:15.220
I thought you were breaking for lunch

00:47:15.220 --> 00:47:16.713
like half an hour ago.

00:47:17.695 --> 00:47:19.455
What's going on?

00:47:19.455 --> 00:47:23.236
- Well, these people are detectives.

00:47:23.236 --> 00:47:24.860
- Real ones?

00:47:24.860 --> 00:47:25.693
- Yes, ma'am.

00:47:25.693 --> 00:47:26.563
Well, you know, I am.

00:47:26.563 --> 00:47:28.830
- It's really quite striking in person.

00:47:28.830 --> 00:47:30.033
Luminous actually.

00:47:31.316 --> 00:47:32.280
- Thank you.

00:47:32.280 --> 00:47:33.880
- Interesting, I've never
been very fond of you

00:47:33.880 --> 00:47:34.863
on the big screen.

00:47:36.360 --> 00:47:37.193
- Thank you?

00:47:37.193 --> 00:47:38.026
- I'm sorry.

00:47:38.026 --> 00:47:39.563
Lucifer Morningstar.

00:47:41.480 --> 00:47:43.650
- Oh, wow, great name.

00:47:43.650 --> 00:47:45.170
What is this all about?

00:47:45.170 --> 00:47:47.513
- Oh we have some questions about Delilah.

00:47:49.750 --> 00:47:51.040
- Oh, yes.

00:47:51.040 --> 00:47:52.613
That's so sad.

00:47:52.613 --> 00:47:53.946
- Yes, very sad.

00:47:56.352 --> 00:48:00.143
- (laughing) Your watch,
where'd you get it?

00:48:02.129 --> 00:48:04.392
- It's a prop.

00:48:04.392 --> 00:48:07.293
- No, that's the one
Delilah gave you, isn't it?

00:48:08.630 --> 00:48:10.030
For "Time Will Tell"?

00:48:10.030 --> 00:48:11.027
- Oh, right.

00:48:12.227 --> 00:48:13.910
That's the movie we did.

00:48:13.910 --> 00:48:16.053
It was a wrap gift.

00:48:16.970 --> 00:48:20.463
- She gave a $10,000
watch to the whole crew?

00:48:21.390 --> 00:48:22.480
- Oh no, just me.

00:48:22.480 --> 00:48:24.213
As far as I know.

00:48:25.550 --> 00:48:30.160
We were, you know, costars and everything.

00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:31.030
- You'll have to lie better than that

00:48:31.030 --> 00:48:33.150
if you want to be president,
(coughing) excuse me.

00:48:33.150 --> 00:48:34.333
- I know, right?

00:48:35.230 --> 00:48:36.930
- So you were sleeping with her then.

00:48:36.930 --> 00:48:37.793
- Oh yeah.

00:48:40.150 --> 00:48:41.780
- I can hear you.

00:48:41.780 --> 00:48:42.653
- So can I.

00:48:43.816 --> 00:48:46.658
- I just said that out loud, didn't I?

00:48:46.658 --> 00:48:47.499
- Uh huh.

00:48:47.499 --> 00:48:49.068
- In front of people.

00:48:49.068 --> 00:48:50.498
Police people.

00:48:50.498 --> 00:48:51.940
Whatever, not like I didn't know.

00:48:51.940 --> 00:48:56.810
And Grey, you're a terrible
liar and actor by the way.

00:48:56.810 --> 00:48:58.179
- You knew?

00:48:58.179 --> 00:48:59.360
- Of course!

00:48:59.360 --> 00:49:01.619
Why do you think I've
been sleeping with Bobby?

00:49:01.619 --> 00:49:05.380
- (gasping) Are you serious?

00:49:05.380 --> 00:49:06.400
- Oh yeah.

00:49:06.400 --> 00:49:09.490
And let me tell you, it's good.

00:49:09.490 --> 00:49:11.917
I climb that man like a tree.

00:49:11.917 --> 00:49:13.930
(woman laughing)

00:49:13.930 --> 00:49:15.380
- My bodyguard?

00:49:15.380 --> 00:49:16.835
What a cliche.

00:49:16.835 --> 00:49:18.043
- Oh, okay.

00:49:19.623 --> 00:49:20.790
I'm a cliche.

00:49:21.740 --> 00:49:23.095
Well you're a dick.

00:49:23.095 --> 00:49:26.130
(everyone laughing)

00:49:26.130 --> 00:49:27.230
- Arrest them.

00:49:27.230 --> 00:49:29.420
One of them's gotta be guilty.

00:49:29.420 --> 00:49:30.370
- Well, that was fun.

00:49:32.086 --> 00:49:34.200
- Everybody fights.

00:49:34.200 --> 00:49:35.238
And now,

00:49:35.238 --> 00:49:36.870
(everyone laughing)

00:49:36.870 --> 00:49:39.400
- I read somebody's part, I'm so sorry.

00:49:39.400 --> 00:49:40.410
- Now Chloe can't help

00:49:40.410 --> 00:49:43.639
but crack the slightest
smug smile at this time.

00:49:43.639 --> 00:49:46.513
And they watch the
chaos they both created.

00:49:48.350 --> 00:49:51.880
Exterior Lux, street, night.

00:49:51.880 --> 00:49:53.950
A vigil honoring Delilah on the sidewalk,

00:49:53.950 --> 00:49:56.760
candles and letters
around a small TV playing

00:49:56.760 --> 00:49:59.070
one of Delilah's performances.

00:49:59.070 --> 00:50:00.580
Now we're inside Lux, night.

00:50:00.580 --> 00:50:03.280
Chloe's got a beer in one
hand, cell in the other.

00:50:03.280 --> 00:50:04.490
Smug smile gone.

00:50:04.490 --> 00:50:07.083
Lucifer sips his scotch,
spinning that coin.

00:50:08.050 --> 00:50:11.083
Maze stands a few yards away
watching disapprovingly.

00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:13.440
- I know, I know, check again.

00:50:13.440 --> 00:50:16.560
What about their
assistants' phones, nannies,

00:50:16.560 --> 00:50:18.920
fan pages, Twitter?

00:50:18.920 --> 00:50:19.753
Okay.

00:50:19.753 --> 00:50:21.233
Well, call if anything changes.

00:50:22.240 --> 00:50:23.820
Grey and Amanda have zero connection

00:50:23.820 --> 00:50:25.760
to the shooter or the driver.

00:50:25.760 --> 00:50:26.810
Maybe Dan was right.

00:50:26.810 --> 00:50:28.920
Maybe the shooter wasn't
working for anyone.

00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:31.350
Maybe this does start and end with him.

00:50:31.350 --> 00:50:33.730
- No, I don't believe it.

00:50:33.730 --> 00:50:36.550
- He did have the same damn watch as Grey.

00:50:36.550 --> 00:50:37.470
Can't be a coincidence.

00:50:37.470 --> 00:50:40.370
Maybe Delilah gave it to him too,

00:50:40.370 --> 00:50:42.256
kind of her go-to gift.

00:50:42.256 --> 00:50:45.510
- Well, that would imply she
was sleeping with that maggot.

00:50:45.510 --> 00:50:49.540
- Let's see, Jimmy, 2Vile, Grey Cooper.

00:50:49.540 --> 00:50:51.540
She was sleeping with three other maggots.

00:50:51.540 --> 00:50:54.500
Not like she has tremendous discretion.

00:50:54.500 --> 00:50:55.950
God, why am I here?

00:50:55.950 --> 00:50:59.490
- Wrong deity, but that is the
eternal question, isn't it?

00:50:59.490 --> 00:51:02.817
- No, I mean here, in a bar with you.

00:51:02.817 --> 00:51:04.903
- Well I don't know, Detective.

00:51:05.800 --> 00:51:07.580
Despite your proclaimed revulsion,

00:51:07.580 --> 00:51:10.350
you can't deny there's
a connection between us.

00:51:10.350 --> 00:51:12.000
Tell me, what do you really want?

00:51:15.260 --> 00:51:16.780
- You mean, what do I desire more

00:51:16.780 --> 00:51:18.360
than anything else in this life?

00:51:18.360 --> 00:51:19.890
- Hmm, yes.

00:51:19.890 --> 00:51:20.820
No tricks.

00:51:20.820 --> 00:51:23.299
Not that they work with
you anyway, you freak.

00:51:23.299 --> 00:51:25.233
Just tell me, I'm curious.

00:51:27.681 --> 00:51:31.310
- I suppose what I was saying
before, you know, to you

00:51:31.310 --> 00:51:32.283
was kind of true.

00:51:33.295 --> 00:51:34.545
I do want to help people.

00:51:35.640 --> 00:51:37.513
- Ugh, your purity repulses me.

00:51:39.236 --> 00:51:44.236
- Well, your lack of it isn't
wildly attractive either.

00:51:44.270 --> 00:51:46.920
My father was a cop, pretty great one.

00:51:46.920 --> 00:51:49.070
My mother was an actress,
pretty cheesy one.

00:51:49.070 --> 00:51:50.300
And she tried to kill me in a scene

00:51:50.300 --> 00:51:51.680
with a glass, just kidding.

00:51:51.680 --> 00:51:53.050
I tried the acting thing.

00:51:53.050 --> 00:51:55.360
I took my top off.

00:51:55.360 --> 00:51:58.122
Not exactly contributing to
the betterment of society.

00:51:58.122 --> 00:51:59.039
- Disagree.

00:52:00.340 --> 00:52:01.410
- Anyway.

00:52:01.410 --> 00:52:04.130
Didn't like how it made
me feel about myself.

00:52:04.130 --> 00:52:04.963
So I quit.

00:52:04.963 --> 00:52:07.200
I became a cop like my old man,

00:52:07.200 --> 00:52:09.930
dealt with the whole Hot
Tub High School thing

00:52:09.930 --> 00:52:11.540
till I became a detective

00:52:11.540 --> 00:52:14.430
and found a whole new
way to ostracize myself.

00:52:14.430 --> 00:52:16.170
- Ah, the reason your ex-maggot

00:52:16.170 --> 00:52:17.720
was pressuring you to close this.

00:52:18.670 --> 00:52:19.620
- Yeah.

00:52:19.620 --> 00:52:21.430
A few months ago, I saw a case differently

00:52:21.430 --> 00:52:25.080
than a lot of people in my
department including my ex.

00:52:25.080 --> 00:52:26.380
I stuck my neck out.

00:52:26.380 --> 00:52:27.660
It backfired.

00:52:27.660 --> 00:52:29.130
Now it seems like most of them hate me

00:52:29.130 --> 00:52:30.780
and nobody wants to work with me.

00:52:31.820 --> 00:52:33.760
- Chloe shakes her head,
but can't help but smile.

00:52:33.760 --> 00:52:35.530
Maze interrupts to grab the glasses

00:52:35.530 --> 00:52:38.060
when a familiar music clip plays.

00:52:38.060 --> 00:52:39.930
- Too bad your little protege's not around

00:52:39.930 --> 00:52:40.913
to cash the check.

00:52:43.090 --> 00:52:44.500
- [Chloe] Wow.

00:52:44.500 --> 00:52:45.917
- [Lucifer] What?

00:52:46.790 --> 00:52:49.490
- Delilah didn't get that watch to Eddie.

00:52:49.490 --> 00:52:51.180
- Interior recording
studio later that night.

00:52:51.180 --> 00:52:53.360
Late night session, a
young boy band recording.

00:52:53.360 --> 00:52:55.120
Tired mixers at work

00:52:55.120 --> 00:52:58.430
and Jimmy harping on a Justin Biebery kid.

00:52:58.430 --> 00:53:01.310
Door booms open, techs and mixers curse,

00:53:01.310 --> 00:53:03.630
as Lucifer and Chloe interrupt the session

00:53:03.630 --> 00:53:05.690
making a beeline for Jimmy.

00:53:05.690 --> 00:53:08.113
- Hello Jimmy, how are
the album sales doing?

00:53:09.272 --> 00:53:10.560
- Ready, Tom?

00:53:10.560 --> 00:53:12.193
- Oh, yes please, hit me.

00:53:13.340 --> 00:53:15.200
- I believe Whitney
Houston reached the top 10

00:53:15.200 --> 00:53:16.740
for album sales after her death.

00:53:16.740 --> 00:53:18.940
Michael Jackson hit the stratosphere.

00:53:18.940 --> 00:53:21.240
Having Delilah killed,

00:53:21.240 --> 00:53:23.930
you're bound to reach at least the top 20.

00:53:23.930 --> 00:53:27.670
That's a truckload of royalty
checks coming your way.

00:53:27.670 --> 00:53:29.690
Guess you need that cash, huh?

00:53:29.690 --> 00:53:32.490
Which is why you had to pay
the shooter with your watch.

00:53:32.490 --> 00:53:34.167
- The watch Delilah gave you.

00:53:34.167 --> 00:53:35.620
Now that's just sick

00:53:35.620 --> 00:53:37.820
but then you are so...

00:53:37.820 --> 00:53:39.240
- Jimmy's sweaty face turns red.

00:53:39.240 --> 00:53:41.240
He grabs one of the boy bands as a shield

00:53:41.240 --> 00:53:43.080
and whips out a fucking gun!

00:53:43.080 --> 00:53:45.064
Chloe's gun is out in a blink.

00:53:45.064 --> 00:53:46.260
- Whoa!

00:53:46.260 --> 00:53:47.663
Whoa, whoa, hey Jimmy.

00:53:48.503 --> 00:53:50.630
- I made her!

00:53:50.630 --> 00:53:52.597
And she ruined me!

00:53:53.514 --> 00:53:55.014
She humiliated me!

00:53:56.590 --> 00:53:57.897
She owes me!

00:53:57.897 --> 00:53:59.860
- You're not God, Jimmy.

00:53:59.860 --> 00:54:01.432
You didn't make her.

00:54:01.432 --> 00:54:02.620
But you did destroy her

00:54:02.620 --> 00:54:03.970
so I'm going to punish you.

00:54:05.790 --> 00:54:07.780
- Back off, you freak!

00:54:07.780 --> 00:54:09.327
I mean it!

00:54:09.327 --> 00:54:12.530
I'm not going to prison for that bitch.

00:54:12.530 --> 00:54:14.460
No fucking chance!

00:54:14.460 --> 00:54:15.799
- Oh shit.
- Listen to him.

00:54:15.799 --> 00:54:17.340
Back off.

00:54:17.340 --> 00:54:19.870
- It's fine, I told you I'm immortal.

00:54:19.870 --> 00:54:20.730
- Jimmy's twitchy.

00:54:20.730 --> 00:54:22.700
Lucifer gets too close and
Jimmy's swings his gun up

00:54:22.700 --> 00:54:24.143
to fire on Lucifer and boom!

00:54:25.004 --> 00:54:26.750
Chloe gets off two shots first.

00:54:26.750 --> 00:54:29.100
One hits a lamp, the other nails Jimmy.

00:54:29.100 --> 00:54:31.260
He drops to the ground dead.

00:54:31.260 --> 00:54:32.683
And here's the fun part.

00:54:32.683 --> 00:54:34.805
Lucifer's pissed.

00:54:34.805 --> 00:54:36.003
- Why did you do that?

00:54:38.130 --> 00:54:39.087
- He was going to kill you.

00:54:39.087 --> 00:54:41.300
- No, no, no, you just
let him off too easy.

00:54:41.300 --> 00:54:43.080
He needs to suffer, he needs to pay,

00:54:43.080 --> 00:54:46.113
he needs to feel the pain, not escape it.

00:54:47.030 --> 00:54:48.730
- Well, I mean, don't worry.

00:54:48.730 --> 00:54:51.490
I'm sure where he's going,
the punishment's coming. -

00:54:51.490 --> 00:54:53.110
- Actually, no it's not.

00:54:53.110 --> 00:54:54.280
And why?

00:54:54.280 --> 00:54:55.859
Because I'm here, and he-

00:54:55.859 --> 00:54:57.220
- Boom, boom, boom!

00:54:57.220 --> 00:54:59.950
All eyes were off Jimmy
who was still ticking

00:54:59.950 --> 00:55:01.520
and fires off three shots of Chloe.

00:55:01.520 --> 00:55:02.353
One lands.

00:55:02.353 --> 00:55:03.186
Chloe goes down.

00:55:03.186 --> 00:55:04.290
- No!

00:55:04.290 --> 00:55:06.090
- Chloe staggers, blood coming up fast.

00:55:06.090 --> 00:55:07.523
Lucifer hurries to her side.

00:55:08.510 --> 00:55:10.343
- I don't want to die.

00:55:11.644 --> 00:55:12.544
- I won't let you.

00:55:13.790 --> 00:55:16.130
My father will just have to wait for you.

00:55:16.130 --> 00:55:18.280
- The moment is interrupted
by more shots from Jimmy.

00:55:18.280 --> 00:55:19.510
Lucifer protects Chloe now

00:55:19.510 --> 00:55:21.486
using his own body as a shield.

00:55:21.486 --> 00:55:23.287
- Jimmy is crazy.

00:55:23.287 --> 00:55:25.330
(everyone laughing)

00:55:25.330 --> 00:55:27.103
- That's right, motherfuckers!

00:55:28.604 --> 00:55:30.310
- Wait here just a second.

00:55:30.310 --> 00:55:32.350
- Lucifer turns and we stay in Chloe's POV

00:55:32.350 --> 00:55:33.820
her vision blurred, distorted.

00:55:33.820 --> 00:55:34.920
She's catching only glimpses

00:55:34.920 --> 00:55:36.250
but sees Lucifer walk over,

00:55:36.250 --> 00:55:37.390
grab Jimmy by the neck

00:55:37.390 --> 00:55:40.450
and slam him up against
the nearby glass booth.

00:55:40.450 --> 00:55:42.100
The glass cracks in a spider web

00:55:42.100 --> 00:55:44.640
and we see Lucifer's broken demonic face

00:55:44.640 --> 00:55:47.040
in the shattered glass behind Jimmy.

00:55:47.040 --> 00:55:50.073
- Please don't kill me.

00:55:51.650 --> 00:55:53.950
- You're gonna wish that
was all I did to you.

00:55:54.957 --> 00:55:56.890
- And then Chloe's vision is lost to black

00:55:56.890 --> 00:55:58.990
and we hear Jimmy's blood curdling scream.

00:56:01.256 --> 00:56:03.420
Over that moment of darkness

00:56:03.420 --> 00:56:06.810
which then gives away to
a bright tunnel of light.

00:56:06.810 --> 00:56:08.190
Oh wait, it's just regular light.

00:56:08.190 --> 00:56:10.250
A hospital bed light.

00:56:10.250 --> 00:56:11.990
Interior hospital room, day.

00:56:11.990 --> 00:56:13.330
Chloe is coming to.

00:56:13.330 --> 00:56:16.573
We find Lucifer hovering over her.

00:56:16.573 --> 00:56:18.273
- Well, look who's back.

00:56:19.890 --> 00:56:21.273
- How long have I been out?

00:56:22.110 --> 00:56:23.123
- Three years.

00:56:24.299 --> 00:56:27.299
(everyone laughing)

00:56:28.420 --> 00:56:29.683
- You're such an ass.

00:56:31.940 --> 00:56:33.590
He was firing at you.

00:56:33.590 --> 00:56:36.997
Why are you not more dead?

00:56:36.997 --> 00:56:38.030
- You're having a very hard time

00:56:38.030 --> 00:56:40.043
with the whole immortal thing, aren't you?

00:56:41.906 --> 00:56:44.490
- I must have been delirious
from the blood loss.

00:56:44.490 --> 00:56:47.120
- Well, whatever helps you sleep, my dear.

00:56:47.120 --> 00:56:48.413
- What happened to Jimmy?

00:56:49.419 --> 00:56:51.586
- He got what he deserved.

00:56:52.522 --> 00:56:55.110
- Well, I am pretty sure I'd be dead

00:56:55.110 --> 00:56:56.730
if you hadn't have helped me.

00:56:56.730 --> 00:56:58.363
So, thank you.

00:57:00.290 --> 00:57:02.560
- Sorry, I missed that last part.

00:57:02.560 --> 00:57:03.493
- Thank you!

00:57:04.900 --> 00:57:06.490
- You're welcome.

00:57:06.490 --> 00:57:09.603
Besides, you're far too
interesting to let die.

00:57:10.830 --> 00:57:13.740
- You saved my life because
you find me interesting?

00:57:13.740 --> 00:57:15.663
- Wildly irritating as well, but yes.

00:57:18.530 --> 00:57:19.643
- So now what?

00:57:20.656 --> 00:57:22.610
- Well, obviously I've proved myself

00:57:22.610 --> 00:57:25.080
as an invaluable crime fighting tool.

00:57:25.080 --> 00:57:26.550
You were a pariah in the department.

00:57:26.550 --> 00:57:27.400
I think this is the beginning

00:57:27.400 --> 00:57:29.250
of a beautiful friendship, don't you?

00:57:30.630 --> 00:57:32.270
- Who the hell are you?

00:57:32.270 --> 00:57:33.103
- I told you.

00:57:33.950 --> 00:57:34.830
I'm-

00:57:34.830 --> 00:57:36.260
- Lucifer!

00:57:36.260 --> 00:57:39.121
- [Joe] It's Trixie,
ex-husband Dan in tow.

00:57:39.121 --> 00:57:41.360
- Oh, now now.

00:57:41.360 --> 00:57:42.830
That's enough, child.

00:57:42.830 --> 00:57:45.280
Save some of this
unpleasantness for your mother.

00:57:47.600 --> 00:57:48.570
I think she's one hell

00:57:48.570 --> 00:57:50.327
of a homicide detective, don't you?

00:57:51.610 --> 00:57:54.550
- Uh yeah, she is.

00:57:54.550 --> 00:57:55.623
I'm happy for you.

00:57:56.810 --> 00:57:58.043
- Yeah, thanks.

00:58:00.370 --> 00:58:02.643
- I'm trying to compliment you here.

00:58:03.530 --> 00:58:04.840
- Okay.

00:58:04.840 --> 00:58:06.320
I will take it.

00:58:06.320 --> 00:58:07.410
Thank you.

00:58:07.410 --> 00:58:08.560
- You're welcome.

00:58:08.560 --> 00:58:13.170
- I bet the department's
surfing. (laughing)

00:58:13.170 --> 00:58:14.653
Dan, are you okay?

00:58:16.040 --> 00:58:16.900
- I'm being a douche,

00:58:16.900 --> 00:58:18.290
that's my version of a douche.

00:58:18.290 --> 00:58:19.123
- I love it.

00:58:19.123 --> 00:58:20.140
- It feels like Kevin's here, so.

00:58:20.140 --> 00:58:22.323
- Yeah it's just like Kevin actually.

00:58:23.790 --> 00:58:24.940
Spot on.

00:58:24.940 --> 00:58:25.773
- Uncanny.

00:58:28.550 --> 00:58:29.383
Where were we?

00:58:30.970 --> 00:58:31.803
- Top of 37.

00:58:31.803 --> 00:58:34.300
- Yeah, but you need to be more careful.

00:58:34.300 --> 00:58:36.640
- Yeah, but you need to be more careful.

00:58:36.640 --> 00:58:38.860
You should've had backup.

00:58:38.860 --> 00:58:40.203
- She had backup.

00:58:42.100 --> 00:58:43.650
- Thank you,

00:58:43.650 --> 00:58:45.295
for helping her.

00:58:45.295 --> 00:58:48.270
- (sighing) It's hard for you, isn't it?

00:58:48.270 --> 00:58:49.383
Not to be a douche.

00:58:51.360 --> 00:58:52.670
Well I'd stay for the family reunion,

00:58:52.670 --> 00:58:54.710
but it's given me terrible IBS.

00:58:54.710 --> 00:58:57.030
Look forward to seeing you soon, Chloe.

00:58:57.030 --> 00:58:57.863
- I don't.

00:58:57.863 --> 00:58:59.010
- Bye now.

00:58:59.010 --> 00:59:00.450
Glad you're not dead.

00:59:00.450 --> 00:59:01.283
- Yeah.

00:59:01.283 --> 00:59:03.670
- Lucifer leaves but
looks back for a moment,

00:59:03.670 --> 00:59:06.170
curious as to why he gives a good god damn

00:59:06.170 --> 00:59:07.430
about any of them.

00:59:07.430 --> 00:59:08.910
He frowns, troubled.

00:59:08.910 --> 00:59:10.340
Exterior Lux, street, night.

00:59:10.340 --> 00:59:11.940
Lucifer pulls up, gets out,

00:59:11.940 --> 00:59:13.960
handing his keys to the valet
who greets him with a smile

00:59:13.960 --> 00:59:15.780
and says nothing

00:59:15.780 --> 00:59:17.946
because he has just
slipped into slow motion.

00:59:17.946 --> 00:59:19.529
- Ugh, bloody hell.

00:59:22.060 --> 00:59:23.393
What do you want from me?

00:59:24.420 --> 00:59:26.040
- I've been watching you, Lucifer.

00:59:26.040 --> 00:59:26.873
- Perv.

00:59:29.144 --> 00:59:32.030
- I'm not sure that I like what I see.

00:59:32.030 --> 00:59:35.210
You've been showing restraint, mercy.

00:59:35.210 --> 00:59:38.000
- I'm scared I'm turning
away from the dark side, bro.

00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:40.240
Going to give you a little
competition for dad's fave?

00:59:40.240 --> 00:59:41.920
Don't worry, I'm not.

00:59:41.920 --> 00:59:43.533
- Oh, I don't believe you.

00:59:44.380 --> 00:59:48.420
The human world can be even
more painful than hell, Lucifer.

00:59:48.420 --> 00:59:50.360
Stay here and prepare to feel things

00:59:50.360 --> 00:59:52.640
you have never felt before.

00:59:52.640 --> 00:59:54.672
- Don't threaten me, Amenadiel.

00:59:54.672 --> 00:59:55.940
You won't win.

00:59:55.940 --> 00:59:57.153
- Then go back.

00:59:58.740 --> 01:00:00.440
- You're the one who's threatened.

01:00:01.810 --> 01:00:03.163
- Oh, Luci.

01:00:04.100 --> 01:00:07.650
My hatred of you grow
stronger with every visit.

01:00:07.650 --> 01:00:10.050
- Wouldn't have it any other way, pal.

01:00:10.050 --> 01:00:12.230
Look forward to eating your heart one day.

01:00:12.230 --> 01:00:13.063
Peace.

01:00:14.260 --> 01:00:16.340
- Amenadiel turns and walks off.

01:00:16.340 --> 01:00:17.520
Lucifer watches him go.

01:00:17.520 --> 01:00:19.250
These two brothers will never, ever,

01:00:19.250 --> 01:00:22.215
ever be close.

01:00:22.215 --> 01:00:25.850
Interior (everyone laughing)

01:00:25.850 --> 01:00:27.940
Interior Lux, moments later.

01:00:27.940 --> 01:00:29.350
That was my narrating, by the way.

01:00:29.350 --> 01:00:30.700
Lucifer drops down at the piano.

01:00:30.700 --> 01:00:32.180
Maze watces from a short distance.

01:00:32.180 --> 01:00:33.870
What looks like a dagger
spins on its point

01:00:33.870 --> 01:00:35.280
in the palm of her hand.

01:00:35.280 --> 01:00:36.890
But before we get a
good luck, she stops it,

01:00:36.890 --> 01:00:38.343
walks over to Lucifer quiet.

01:00:39.370 --> 01:00:41.420
- Hints of disapproval, Maze, what is it?

01:00:42.680 --> 01:00:45.853
- I just can understand why
you would save a human life.

01:00:47.200 --> 01:00:49.130
- There's something different about her.

01:00:49.130 --> 01:00:52.200
Something I can't figure
out and it vexes me.

01:00:52.200 --> 01:00:54.527
- Maybe it's not her that's different.

01:00:55.840 --> 01:00:57.990
- Is this where I ask
whatever do you mean?

01:00:58.960 --> 01:01:00.890
- Stop caring.

01:01:00.890 --> 01:01:01.793
You're the devil.

01:01:03.180 --> 01:01:04.013
- Yes.

01:01:05.160 --> 01:01:06.609
Yes, I am.

01:01:06.609 --> 01:01:07.760
- But there's doubt in his eyes

01:01:07.760 --> 01:01:09.955
as he launches into an
eerie instrumental rendition

01:01:09.955 --> 01:01:12.760
of "Gimme Shelter", which continues over

01:01:12.760 --> 01:01:15.140
into your therapist's
office, waiting room, day.

01:01:15.140 --> 01:01:16.790
Dr. Linda Martin sits in her office

01:01:16.790 --> 01:01:18.640
as she notices a little red
light blinking over a door.

01:01:18.640 --> 01:01:19.630
She's confused.

01:01:19.630 --> 01:01:20.950
Doesn't have an appointment right now.

01:01:20.950 --> 01:01:23.020
She gets up, opens the door.

01:01:23.020 --> 01:01:25.660
Linda startles cause Lucifer's
standing right there.

01:01:25.660 --> 01:01:26.493
- Here's the deal.

01:01:26.493 --> 01:01:29.010
We can have as much naked
cuddle time as you desire

01:01:29.010 --> 01:01:30.480
but I need you to listen to me too.

01:01:30.480 --> 01:01:33.770
I have a few things I'd
like to discuss with you.

01:01:33.770 --> 01:01:35.453
An existential dilemma or two.

01:01:36.340 --> 01:01:37.173
Deal?

01:01:38.040 --> 01:01:39.670
- Linda smiles, deal.

01:01:39.670 --> 01:01:40.790
And as the door shuts behind,

01:01:40.790 --> 01:01:41.700
we smash to black

01:01:41.700 --> 01:01:44.160
and Van Halen's "Running
With The Devil" kicks in.

01:01:44.160 --> 01:01:45.200
On a show that,

01:01:45.200 --> 01:01:47.080
I don't know, the devil solving crimes.

01:01:47.080 --> 01:01:47.930
- I know, never gonna work.
- I don't see it

01:01:47.930 --> 01:01:48.930
lasting a season.

01:01:48.930 --> 01:01:50.326
- Will it get picked up?

01:01:50.326 --> 01:01:52.052
Will it get picked up?
- End of pilot!

01:01:52.052 --> 01:01:52.885
(clapping)

01:01:52.885 --> 01:01:54.602
- It's got three years tops.

01:01:54.602 --> 01:01:57.880
(actors laughing)

01:01:57.880 --> 01:01:59.530
- You guys, that was awesome!

01:01:59.530 --> 01:02:02.113
And it is so nice to
see all of your faces.

01:02:03.040 --> 01:02:04.900
- Nice!
- Mwah, mwah, mwah.

01:02:04.900 --> 01:02:06.020
- Bye, guys.

01:02:06.020 --> 01:02:07.376
- Hi, bye.

01:02:07.376 --> 01:02:09.950
- Thanks for watching, guys.
- Thanks, everybody.

01:02:09.950 --> 01:02:11.540
- We love you, take care.

01:02:11.540 --> 01:02:12.850
- Love you guys, bye.

01:02:12.850 --> 01:02:14.696
- Bye.
- Bye, everybody.

01:02:14.696 --> 01:02:17.220
(electronic music)

